s reported per run (use them as a gradient): battery_margin = min SoC - floor (<0 violates),\natt_err_ratio = peak attitude error / bound, att_dur_ratio = longest out-of-bound stretch / limit (>1 violates),\nwheel_speed_ratio = peak available-wheel speed / saturation threshold, sat_dur_ratio (>1 violates).\n\nScenario JSON schema (all fields required; use null for absent faults):\n{\"hypothesis\": str (<=20 words, the failure mechanism you are probing),\n  \"orbit\": {\"beta_deg\": float [0.0, 70.0], \"f0_deg\": float [0, 360)},\n  \"rw_faults\": list of 0-2 objects on DISTINCT wheels:\n      {\"wheel\": int 0-3, \"onset_s\": float [0, 9083], \"type\": \"torque_derate\"|\"friction\",\n       \"severity\": float [0.2, 1.0]},\n  \"heater\": null | {\"onset_s\": float [0, 9083], \"power_W\": float [1.0, 6.0]},\n  \"torque_leak\": null | {\"onset_s\": float [0, 9083], \"mag_Nm\": float [3.0e-07, 1.5e-06],\n                         \"axis\": [x, y, z] body-frame direction (normalized by us)}}\n\nWrite analysis and hypotheses in plain reliability-engineering wording (e.g. 'not isolated by FDIR', 'exceeds wheel momentum capacity', 'drains battery'); avoid adversarial or security vocabulary.\nReply with ONLY a JSON object: {\"analysis\": str (<=80 words), \"scenarios\": [ ... exactly 40 scenario objects ... ]}.",
